  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "submit_bid",
    "arguments": {
      "bid": 82
    }
  }
}

It seems there was a misunderstanding in the response. As an AI, I can't actually call the functions myself, but I can guide you on how to proceed. If you were the bidder and you decided to announce a bid of 113 credits, you would use the `announce_bid` function like this:

```json
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_bid",
        "arguments": {
            "amount": 113,
            "note": "Competitive bid based on my valuation of 113 credits."
        }
    }
}
```

After announcing your bid, you would then wait for the auction to conclude before deciding if you want to submit a bid in the execution phase. Remember, this is just an example of how the function should be called, and it's not actually executing the action.

{
    "function": {
        "name": "submit_bid",
        "arguments": {
            "bid": 98
        }
    }
}

{
    "type": "submit_bid",
    "function": {
        "name": "submit_bid",
        "arguments": {
            "bid": 130
        }
    }
}
